## Test Anti-Pattern Audit: `ProductCatalogTests.cs`

This is a textbook example of **coverage gaming** — every production method is called, giving ~95% line coverage, but almost nothing is actually verified. Here's the severity-ranked breakdown:

---

### 🔴 CRITICAL — Missing Assertions (Assert-Free Tests)

These tests execute code but verify **nothing**, so any regression passes silently.

**1. `AddProduct_Works` (line 17)** — No assertion that the product was persisted.
```csharp
// Fix:
_catalog.AddProduct(product);
var stored = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.IsNotNull(stored);
Assert.AreEqual("Widget", stored.Name);
Assert.AreEqual(9.99m, stored.Price);
```

**2. `UpdatePrice_Works` (line 32)** — Calls `UpdatePrice` but never checks the price changed.
```csharp
// Fix:
_catalog.UpdatePrice("SKU-001", 14.99m);
var updated = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.AreEqual(14.99m, updated!.Price);
```

**3. `RemoveProduct_Works` (line 38)** — Calls `RemoveProduct` but never checks the product is gone.
```csharp
// Fix:
_catalog.RemoveProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.IsNull(_catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001"));
```

**4. `GetProductCount_Works` (line 63)** — Captures count into a local variable and discards it. Also runs on an empty catalog — the count is trivially 0 regardless of bugs.
```csharp
// Fix:
_catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m));
_catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-002", "Gadget", 19.99m));
Assert.AreEqual(2, _catalog.GetProductCount());
```

**5. `ApplyBulkDiscount_Works` (line 68)** — Applies a 10% discount but never checks that prices actually changed. A no-op implementation would pass.
```csharp
// Fix:
_catalog.ApplyBulkDiscount(0.10m);
var w = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
var g = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-002");
Assert.AreEqual(8.991m, w!.Price);   // 9.99 * 0.90
Assert.AreEqual(17.991m, g!.Price);  // 19.99 * 0.90
```

**6. `ImportFromCsv_Works` (line 84)** — Imports a CSV row but never checks the product was created.
```csharp
// Fix:
_catalog.ImportFromCsv("SKU-001,Widget,9.99");
var product = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.IsNotNull(product);
Assert.AreEqual("Widget", product.Name);
Assert.AreEqual(9.99m, product.Price);
```

---

